@startuml workspace-reconnect-flow
title Reconnect-on-Save, Not Hot-Swap (CP4)

skinparam defaultFontName Monospaced
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #888888
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam sequenceGroupBorderColor #CCCCCC
skinparam sequenceGroupBodyBackgroundColor #FAFAFA

actor Operator as Op
participant "saveWorkspaceScope()\n(dashboard, CP4)" as Save #E0E7FF
participant "liveSocket.ts\n(dashboard, CP4 adds\nforceReconnect)" as Sock #DBEAFE
participant "API" as API #DBEAFE
database "user_workspaces" as DB #FEF9C3

Op -> Save : (future CP5 UI) submits an edited scope
Save -> API : PUT /users/me/workspace { ...new scope }
API -> DB : INSERT ... ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE
DB --> API : row written
API --> Save : 200 { scope }

alt save failed (4xx/5xx)
  Save -> Save : throw -- forceReconnect() never called
  note right of Save
    The existing connection, and whatever scope
    it already loaded, is left completely alone.
    A failed save must never disturb a working
    connection.
  end note
else save succeeded
  Save -> Sock : forceReconnect()
  Sock -> Sock : bump generation, open a NEW connection\n(old one not yet closed)
  Sock -> API : new WebSocket upgrade (same sentinel_jwt cookie)
  API -> DB : SELECT scope WHERE user_id = ... (CP3's existing connection-open load)
  DB --> API : the just-saved scope
  Sock -> Sock : close the OLD connection\n(its close handler sees a stale\ngeneration and does nothing)
  Sock -> Op : onReconnect() fires (existing mechanism,\nunchanged since before CP3/CP4)
  note right of Op
    Every widget already listening to
    onReconnect (MapWidget, AlertWidget)
    re-hydrates via REST and re-sends its
    bbox subscribe -- CP4 adds no new
    "restore" code, it reuses this.
  end note
end

@enduml
